    2. On a 30x30 grid, draw 2-3 thin meandering 8-connected contour paths spanning most rows.
       Each path steps diagonally or has short horizontal runs, covering nearly every row.
       Together they partition the bg into 2 large exterior regions and 6-12 interior pockets.
    3. Fill all interior bg pockets (4-connected, touching a long contour component) with contour_color
       to produce the output grid.
    4. Scatter obstacle pixels (4-7% of grid) as singletons/small clusters inside and outside the enclosure.
       Obstacle pixels sit on bg in both input and output (they are never recolored).
    5. Add 3-5 short contour fragments (size 1-4) outside the main enclosure as distractors.
